      "side": 1,
      "message": "The `has_children` Boolean is `true` if the packet has a `_payload_` field _or_ if the packet has child packets.\n\nThat is definitely subtle, but I think that should give the behavior you expect?\n\nThis is handled in `lint.rs` where we have\n\n```rust\n                // Handle packets with a payload field (but without any child packets).\n                for field in fields {\n                    if let FieldDesc::Payload { .. } | FieldDesc::Body { .. } \u003d \u0026field.desc {\n                        scope.children.entry(id.to_string()).or_default();\n                        break;\n                    }\n                }\n\n                // Handle child packets.\n                if let Some(parent_id) \u003d parent_id {\n                    scope.children.entry(parent_id.to_string()).or_default().push(decl);\n                }\n```\n\nand then in `rust.rs` where we have\n\n```rust\n    let has_children \u003d scope.children.contains_key(id);\n```\n\nWould it be easier to read if I rename it to `has_payload`?",
      "parentUuid": "666be566_0ab8ecbc",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 339,
